speechtext:
I rise on a question of privilege, Mr. Speaker. There have been discussions among the House leaders with respect to the most appropriate method of dealing with communications which have been received from all parties regarding testimony given before the Standing Committee on Justice and the Solicitor General relating to police investigations of certain members. Those discussions have included yourself and officers of the House.
This is a matter of grave concern to all of us as members of Parliament and we have searched long and hard for an appropriate solution. We have arrived at a two-part solution which will address the current situation and assist the House and its members in the future.
First, I will propose a motion to be jointly moved and seconded by myself; the member for Windsor West, the Official Opposition House leader; and the member for Kamloops, the New Democratic Party House leader to deal with the request for a question of privilege raised by members from all three Parties. The motion will read as follows:
That the Standing Committee on Elections, Privileges, Procedure and Private Members' Business be empowered to study the rights, immunities and privileges of members of the House of Commons.
We also feel that it is appropriate to review our current practices and therefore following the passage of the motion which I just suggested I would move the following motion, again jointly moved and seconded by myself;

Business of the House
the member for Windsor West, the Official Opposition House leader; and the member for Kamloops, the New Democratic Party House leader:
That a special committee of the House be appointed and empowered to review the Parliament of Canada Act regarding the powers, duty and obligations of the members of the House in relation thereto and regarding the authority, responsibilities and jurisdiction of the Board of Internal Economy;
That the said special committee shall have all powers of a standing committee pursuant to Standing Order 108(1);
That the said special committee shall report its findings and recommendations no later than March 5, 1990;
That the said special committee be chaired by the Deputy Speaker; and that seven additional members be recommended by the striking committee.
I believe, Mr. Speaker, that you have a copy of the first motion.
